WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.560
Hiking, camping and exploring the woods&nbsp;
is a favorite past-time for many children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.080
and adults. But you are in for a big&nbsp;
surprise if you happen to stumble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.800
upon THIS particular expanse of woods -&nbsp;
designated by the foundation as: SCP-4000.&nbsp;

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.440
It’s an extradimensional area occupied&nbsp;
by the Fae - A powerful race of reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.320
warpers believed to have been at war with the&nbsp;
Foundation after the infamous Factory incident.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.880
The woods are their domain, but Foundation&nbsp;
operatives must take a path through it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.120
once every year. However they must&nbsp;
abide by certain rules while inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.680
like never using or answering to names - your&nbsp;
own or any others - while inside SCP-4000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.400
as it gives the mystical&nbsp;
entities great power over you.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.880
One researcher, Dr. Japers, made the mistake of&nbsp;
not taking this seriously - After speaking with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.240
a rabbit man, and responding to the name “fellow&nbsp;
scholar” twice in a row, he was owned by the Fae.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.800
He disappeared after returning from SCP-4000, only&nbsp;
to be replaced by a humble, non-anomalous rabbit.

